"""Session manager — v2.5-shaped interface over a pluggable backend.

In v2.1.16 this has one backend (`LocalBackend`) that reads the long-lived
access token, verifies its Ed25519 signature, mints a session token, decrypts
the `.enc` skill tree, and caches a `SessionRecord` on disk.

In v2.1.18 the `ControlPlaneBackend` will be wired, and `SessionManager`
selects between them based on the stamped URL in `hooks/lib/cp-url.local`
(or `hooks/lib/cp-url`), with unreachable CP → fall back to local per user
directive. Runtime SYNAPTORY_CONTROL_PLANE_URL is ignored.

In v2.5 the `LocalBackend` is deleted; the dispatcher always calls the Go
CLI (`synaptory login --if-needed`) which populates the OS keychain with a
byte-identical `SessionRecord` JSON. Every downstream caller stays on this
module's public surface, so the merge is a module swap, not a rewrite.

Public surface (stable across all versions):
    SessionManager().login(project=...) -> SessionRecord
    SessionManager().whoami(project=...) -> SessionRecord | None
    SessionManager().logout(project=...) -> bool
    SessionManager().activate(plugin_root, project=...) -> dict
        # Full SessionStart flow: login + decrypt tree + stamp watermark +
        # write /tmp/.synaptory-session-root marker. Returns the decrypt
        # summary dict for the hook's status message.
    SessionManager().fetch_skill(name) -> str
        # Used by /synaptory skills sync and by any per-skill fallback.

CLI (for hook scripts):
    session_manager.py login [--project <slug>]
    session_manager.py whoami [--project <slug>]
    session_manager.py logout [--project <slug>]
    session_manager.py activate <plugin_root> [--project <slug>]
    session_manager.py fetch-skill <name>
"""

